    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Health and Human Services spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $16B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department executed 23,478 awards at an average award size of $680K, and obligations fell 25.0% year over year. Fiscal-year totals show a decline from $34.3B in FY21 through $21.3B in FY25 down to $16B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Health and Human Services buy?",
      "a": "Health and Human Services buys a mix of IT services, consulting, research, construction, insurance, and pharmaceuticals. Computer Systems Design Services received $2.5B, Other Computer Related Services received $1.4B, Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services received $1.3B, Research and Development in Biotechnology (except Nanobiotechnology) received $1.1B, Custom Computer Programming Services received $1.1B, and Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing received $550M."
